    <p>By day I run international content operations at <b>KukuFM</b>, where I own the localisation engine behind our expansion into Southeast Asia: dubbing Hindi microdramas into Bahasa Indonesia, building the acquisition slate, and running the performance and influencer marketing that gets them watched. Before that I set up KukuFM&rsquo;s Movies category and ran the marketing for its first film.</p>
    <p>I like the seam where <em>strategy meets operations</em>: where a clever idea meets the unglamorous reality of shipping it at scale, on a deadline, across a language and a culture it was not built for. That is what most of this writing is about.</p>
    <p>I trained as an engineer before I found my way into product, marketing, and media, which is probably why I trust a spreadsheet and distrust it in equal measure. <em>Margin of Error</em> is the name for that habit: strong opinions, honestly held, with the error bars drawn in.</p>
